            <ArticleTitle>Tracheobronchial amyloidosis masquerading as bronchial asthma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>117-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of localized tracheobronchial primary amyloidosis masquerading as &quot;bronchial asthma&quot; is presented. Computed tomography of the chest and fiberoptic bronchoscopy image are included. Tracheobronchial primary amyloidosis is a rare, but potentially curable cause of airway obstruction mimicking asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
